WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.547
What a manager is. You are a manager now, and here is what that means, in plain words.

2
00:00:07.597 --> 00:00:15.055
Before, your job was your own work. Now your job is your team’s work, and the people who do it.

3
00:00:15.105 --> 00:00:18.691
That is the whole change, and it is a big one.

4
00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:26.041
Three things are new. One: you decide. What matters this week, who does what, and what waits.

5
00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:30.625
If you do not decide, the loudest request decides for you.

6
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:31.969
Two: you approve.

7
00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:39.714
Timecards, time off, expenses, and requests now come to you, and Vanderbilt trusts your signature,

8
00:00:39.764 --> 00:00:44.694
so look before you sign. Three: you are responsible for people.

9
00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:52.360
Fair treatment, a safe place to speak up, a chance to grow, and the right help when life happens.

10
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.126
You do not have to know everything.

11
00:00:55.176 --> 00:01:03.030
You have an HCM, an Engagement Consultant, a leave office, and a micro module for every common task.

12
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:10.538
What you do have to do is show up as the manager: decide, approve, and take care of the people.

13
00:01:10.588 --> 00:01:15.913
And one thing a manager is not: the person who does everyone’s work.

14
00:01:15.963 --> 00:01:22.393
When you are tempted to just do it yourself, that is the moment to manage instead.

15
00:01:22.443 --> 00:01:27.294
Next: five ideas the best-known voices on management agree on.

